{
  "world_id": "wld_rain_remembers",
  "name": "The Remembering Valleys",
  "description": "Generations after the powered world went silent, three recovering valley towns and a high pass are linked by the old seedway, a chain of trade paths along which seed grain once flowed freely. A feud between two seedway lineages split those routes, and now the last frost is closing in. A seed-keeper's caravan must cross the valleys, trading grain stock and mending the feud before planting season is lost. Technology is limited to salvaged hand-tools, and nothing powered remains. The tone is wistful but hopeful: ruins and grief sit beside stubborn, tender rebuilding. In this world, grain is believed to remember the rain that first wetted it. Every valley's seed thrives best with its own water, which makes trade a delicate act of trust.",
  "locations": [
    {
      "id": "loc_hollow_ford",
      "name": "Hollow Ford",
      "description": "A river-crossing town built inside the shell of a collapsed highway overpass. Its granary is a rebuilt culvert, and its people keep the caravan's departure ledger."
    },
    {
      "id": "loc_tin_orchard",
      "name": "Tin Orchard",
      "description": "A terraced town where fruit trees grow through rusted roofing sheets that residents have kept as rain-catchers. Its jars of stored valley rain are famous along the seedway."
    },
    {
      "id": "loc_gull_cairn_pass",
